cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use iac-scanner in academic work or a security report, please cite it as below."
title: "iac-scanner: AI-augmented Terraform and AWS CDK security scanner with LLM-generated fixes"
abstract: >-
  iac-scanner is a Python CLI and MCP server that scans Terraform (main.tf)
  and AWS CDK (index.ts/index.js) Infrastructure-as-Code for security and
  best-practice defects and generates fixed code via an LLM (OpenAI,
  Anthropic, GitHub Models, or Ollama). It complements rule-based scanners
  (Checkov, tfsec, KICS) rather than replacing them and offers a hybrid
  mode that grounds LLM findings in Checkov's rule engine.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/alphacrack/iac-scanner"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alphacrack/iac-scanner"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/iac-scanner/"
keywords:
  - infrastructure-as-code
  - terraform
  - aws-cdk
  - security
  - sast
  - devsecops
  - llm
  - langchain
  - sarif
